WEBVTT

00:02.590 --> 00:04.520
Is he really on Mars?

00:04.890 --> 00:06.040
Who?

00:06.040 --> 00:07.270
The suspect.

00:07.760 --> 00:10.940
The one seen at the site of 
Dr. Roy Junghardt's murder.

00:11.230 --> 00:12.680
That red figure.

00:13.810 --> 00:14.700
He's there.

00:14.700 --> 00:15.900
I'm worried.

00:15.900 --> 00:17.620
Well, don't be.

00:18.490 --> 00:22.880
Aletheia, the group that oversees Neans, 
is covering up both murders.

00:23.320 --> 00:25.170
That sounds like typical Aletheia.

00:26.160 --> 00:28.360
Electromagnetic waves were observed

00:28.360 --> 00:30.920
at the time of the second murder, 
just like in Dr. Jung's case.

00:31.330 --> 00:33.590
They said the victim was human, but...

00:33.590 --> 00:36.100
There's a chance the victim was a Nean?

00:36.390 --> 00:39.950
Aletheia wouldn't be on the move 
if a Nean wasn't involved.

00:40.310 --> 00:43.120
The first happened on Earth, 
the second on Mars.

00:43.120 --> 00:45.440
It's just common sense 
to follow that line in an investigation.

00:45.740 --> 00:50.800
Investigator Ash, that doesn't seem like a 
very convincing reason for us to go to Mars.

00:51.920 --> 00:53.500
It's just instinct, okay?

00:54.890 --> 00:58.320
<i>The video appears to become 
distorted in the vicinity</i>

00:58.320 --> 01:00.610
<i>of this individual who seems 
to be the suspect.</i>

01:01.590 --> 01:05.500
It would seem this thing you call 
"instinct" warrants further research.

02:40.720 --> 02:41.510
You're late.

02:41.690 --> 02:42.770
And these are all for you.

02:43.010 --> 02:44.800
Now, don't get mad.

02:50.930 --> 02:51.790
Bro!

02:51.790 --> 02:53.150
Whoa, cool!

02:53.150 --> 02:54.260
I want a picture, too!

02:54.260 --> 02:57.990
Miguel, Emily, don't run 
around inside. It's dangerous.

02:58.310 --> 03:00.100
I'll head over there tomorrow.

03:00.100 --> 03:02.240
You have to see our latest product.

03:08.330 --> 03:10.900
Hold up! I'm getting on!

03:21.130 --> 03:22.680
No fair!

03:22.680 --> 03:26.030
Let me see it! 
You've had it the whole time!

03:26.030 --> 03:27.730
You're too little to use it!

03:27.730 --> 03:28.800
No!

03:28.800 --> 03:31.690
Hey, you two. Take a look at that.

03:32.300 --> 03:34.190
Whoa! What is that?!

03:34.540 --> 03:38.820
That's a Vostok-class second-class 
armored space defense craft.

03:38.820 --> 03:39.770
Vos-what?

03:39.770 --> 03:40.830
A battleship.

03:40.830 --> 03:45.970
During the great war, it traveled around Mars, 
right on the front line,

03:45.970 --> 03:50.070
fighting intense battles around the clock 
against any Usurpers in orbit.

03:50.070 --> 03:51.250
Usurpers?

03:51.730 --> 03:53.630
Once upon a time,

03:54.110 --> 03:57.380
aliens came from far beyond our galaxy.

03:57.380 --> 04:01.880
They were very friendly, 
so mankind called them "Visitors."

04:02.310 --> 04:05.750
After that, more aliens came. However!

04:06.140 --> 04:11.000
These aliens were very mean, 
and they attacked humanity!

04:11.590 --> 04:14.900
So mankind called them "Usurpers."

04:15.380 --> 04:17.650
The humans and Usurpers 
never came to an understanding,

04:17.650 --> 04:20.140
so in the end, a great space war broke out!

04:20.140 --> 04:22.610
Mars was humanity's last line of defense!

04:22.950 --> 04:24.720
Now, look to your right.

04:24.720 --> 04:28.620
You can see the wreckage of the 
weapons used to fight the Usurpers!

04:28.840 --> 04:31.280
It was one terrible battle after another!

04:31.280 --> 04:36.320
Humans made every kind of weapon 
you could imagine to fight the Usurpers!

04:36.320 --> 04:40.060
And do you know what the best, 
most powerful one of all was?

04:40.060 --> 04:40.940
Missiles!

04:40.940 --> 04:41.760
Bzzt.

04:41.760 --> 04:43.770
Beams! Really strong beams!

04:43.770 --> 04:45.140
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

04:45.470 --> 04:47.290
The correct answer is...

04:47.290 --> 04:47.960
Neans!

04:47.960 --> 04:48.980
Neans?

04:48.980 --> 04:53.140
Neans fought alongside 
humans against the Usurpers.

04:53.420 --> 04:54.880
Are you a Nean?

04:54.880 --> 04:56.470
Of course she's not!

04:56.470 --> 04:58.740
Neans have scars on their faces.

05:00.910 --> 05:02.570
Mister, you're a Nean, aren't you?

05:02.570 --> 05:04.390
Have you ever killed someone?

05:06.110 --> 05:09.120
Huey? Kill someone? 
That sure would be scary!

05:09.510 --> 05:10.680
You didn't know?

05:10.680 --> 05:13.540
The Neans have to follow the Asimov Code.

05:14.030 --> 05:15.050
Muffymoff?

05:15.430 --> 05:16.670
The Asimov Code.

05:17.340 --> 05:22.170
It's programmed into our hearts 
that we can't harm humans.

05:22.170 --> 05:23.740
He can't kill people,

05:23.740 --> 05:27.360
but Huey used to be a soldier, 
and he was an absolute star in the war.

05:27.670 --> 05:28.930
When he took on that war machine—

05:28.930 --> 05:31.680
Dear, don't talk about such scary things.

05:31.680 --> 05:33.560
You'll ruin our vacation.

05:34.410 --> 05:37.600
My duty now is serving the mister 
and missus here.

05:37.920 --> 05:41.480
Huey, isn't it about time for your Nectar?

05:41.890 --> 05:43.300
I'm all right for now.

05:43.710 --> 05:45.440
Thank you for your concern.

05:45.900 --> 05:48.700
Ma'am, shall I bring you a blanket?

05:55.800 --> 05:56.670
Just give her some.

06:02.210 --> 06:03.660
Wow. Some grown-up you are.

06:03.660 --> 06:06.480
I'm not a grown-up. 
I'm a precious little child.

06:06.840 --> 06:08.890
I totally get how you feel.

06:09.640 --> 06:12.770
When you love something, 
you don't want anyone else taking it, right?

06:12.770 --> 06:14.660
That's chocolate from Broma, isn't it?

06:14.660 --> 06:15.810
I love that stuff.

06:16.840 --> 06:19.950
And you really know a lot 
about the war on Mars, huh?

06:19.950 --> 06:22.730
Aw, well, I wouldn't say I don't.

06:22.730 --> 06:25.070
Are you, perhaps, a beautiful 
historian of some kind?

06:25.720 --> 06:27.570
She's just a history-loving military nerd.

06:29.700 --> 06:31.400
A student, then?

06:31.760 --> 06:34.120
Yeah, something like that.

06:34.490 --> 06:36.900
Could you maybe stop 
taking pictures, though?

06:37.260 --> 06:39.930
Sorry about that. 
The camera just loves you.

06:39.930 --> 06:41.540
What is that, anyway?

06:42.290 --> 06:43.160
My partner.

06:43.480 --> 06:45.340
That's an optical camera, isn't it?

06:45.340 --> 06:46.820
A camera? It's huge.

06:46.820 --> 06:51.030
It's bulky, moody, 
and the biggest pain in the ass,

06:51.030 --> 06:53.030
but it's saved me so many times.

06:53.030 --> 06:54.840
It's the best partner I could have.

06:55.830 --> 06:57.930
I'm Jill, a journalist.

06:58.320 --> 07:01.330
I've been studying the 
presence of Neans in society.

07:02.110 --> 07:06.300
Mars has a lot of Neans working in combat 
and the development of the planet,

07:06.910 --> 07:09.410
but there are some who face discrimination.

07:09.410 --> 07:11.390
And what about you two?

07:11.390 --> 07:13.180
What brings you to Wellstown?

07:13.670 --> 07:14.550
Um...

07:15.140 --> 07:16.910
We're going after some bad guys.

07:17.200 --> 07:18.040
Bad guys?

07:18.040 --> 07:21.350
That's the premise of this trip we're taking as 
two cringeworthy history-loving military nerds!

07:21.350 --> 07:23.730
Aw, man! Now she knows how cringe we are!

07:26.820 --> 07:28.330
I'm Naomi Orthmann.

07:28.680 --> 07:29.650
Pleasure.

07:30.100 --> 07:30.880
Go on.

07:32.810 --> 07:34.390
Rouge Redstar.

07:36.190 --> 07:36.850
Rouge?

07:37.120 --> 07:38.470
That's a nice name.

07:38.810 --> 07:39.570
Thanks.

07:41.480 --> 07:42.560
A journalist,

07:42.980 --> 07:44.570
a grandma with her grandkids,

07:44.870 --> 07:47.030
tourists and their Nean servant,

07:47.470 --> 07:48.280
a salesman...

07:50.310 --> 07:51.150
and a mystery.

07:51.780 --> 07:55.120
Grandma told us that kids 
can't go by themselves!

07:55.120 --> 07:56.940
But I want to see outside!

07:56.940 --> 07:58.280
Want to go out on the deck?

07:58.280 --> 07:59.730
Why don't we take you?

08:00.690 --> 08:01.540
Yay!

08:01.540 --> 08:02.470
Really?

08:02.470 --> 08:03.950
Yeah, really.

08:03.950 --> 08:07.980
Dah-da-dah! This nice lady 
here will take you!

08:08.410 --> 08:09.220
Cool! Let's go!

08:09.220 --> 08:10.020
Yay!

08:10.020 --> 08:10.920
Wait, I, uh...

08:12.410 --> 08:15.250
They say if you love your kids, 
send them out into the world, right?

08:15.250 --> 08:17.480
Go climb the stairs to adulthood.

08:19.660 --> 08:21.580
I'm gonna show this to my mom.

08:21.580 --> 08:22.380
Your mom?

08:22.830 --> 08:25.040
She's in a hospital in Wellstown.

08:25.430 --> 08:27.320
She can't go outside.

08:28.030 --> 08:30.780
So we're going to show her a bunch of it.

08:34.830 --> 08:37.310
That's it! Gimme back the camera!

08:40.940 --> 08:43.420
Excuse me, sir. What do you do for a living?

08:44.290 --> 08:46.290
No, wait! I'll guess!

08:46.290 --> 08:49.170
I'm doing my first ever 
"guess the occupation" quiz show!

08:50.360 --> 08:51.670
I bet you're...

08:51.940 --> 08:53.110
Hmm...

08:53.920 --> 08:55.510
An assassin for some 
underground organization?

08:56.860 --> 08:59.510
A member of a birding group on Mars? No?

08:59.510 --> 09:01.470
You look like you're pretty smart...

09:01.470 --> 09:04.430
IT stuff? Company president? 
Wait, I'll get it...

09:05.170 --> 09:06.400
Give me a hint!

09:09.390 --> 09:11.150
I work with bodies.

09:14.250 --> 09:15.660
You're a masseur?

09:20.750 --> 09:21.970
Let's go inside.

09:23.570 --> 09:24.790
Target located.

09:25.390 --> 09:26.790
Initiate the operation.

09:26.980 --> 09:29.240
Bring her back alive.

09:29.550 --> 09:30.460
<i>Roger.</i>

09:32.300 --> 09:34.830
Some scary people who seem 
to want us are here.

09:35.420 --> 09:38.050
No, we don't know that yet.

09:38.050 --> 09:40.640
Could just be some military 
nerds out on a jaunt.

09:40.640 --> 09:44.890
So then the doves they let loose are 
instantly toasted by the ray guns...

09:57.850 --> 10:00.370
<i>The bus has made an emergency stop.</i>

10:00.730 --> 10:04.370
<i>All passengers, please follow 
the crew's instructions.</i>

10:04.370 --> 10:06.540
"Crew"? Wait, me?!

10:05.090 --> 10:06.540
<i>All passengers, please...</i>

10:12.870 --> 10:14.450
<i>Hand over the woman shown.</i>

10:14.450 --> 10:17.080
<i>Once our objective is met, 
we will guarantee your safety.</i>

10:17.080 --> 10:19.580
<i>Repeat: hand over the woman shown.</i>

10:19.580 --> 10:22.090
<i>Once our objective is met, 
we will guarantee your safety.</i>

10:21.030 --> 10:22.670
Where did that chick go?!

10:22.670 --> 10:24.060
She was sitting right here!

10:24.060 --> 10:26.980
We can't just hand a girl over 
to those ruffians!

10:26.980 --> 10:28.730
Looks like they're mercenaries.

10:29.070 --> 10:32.270
They said they'll guarantee our safety 
if we hand her over!

10:32.270 --> 10:34.990
Guys like that never keep their word.

10:34.990 --> 10:37.990
We're witnesses. They won't 
let us leave here unharmed.

10:37.990 --> 10:39.490
So what do we do, then?!

10:42.260 --> 10:44.150
Hey! Do something!

10:44.150 --> 10:45.910
What am I supposed to do?!

10:45.910 --> 10:48.240
I haven't driven one of these 
on my own in ages!

10:48.240 --> 10:49.830
Start driving! Hurry!

10:49.830 --> 10:51.400
Uh... Where's the manual...

10:51.400 --> 10:52.130
Oh, just move!

10:53.360 --> 10:54.570
I'll take care of this.

10:54.570 --> 10:57.630
I'd rather not let anyone 
find out who we are.

10:57.630 --> 10:58.900
I'll be careful.

10:59.640 --> 11:01.640
Oh, hell.

11:09.510 --> 11:10.070
Three minutes.

11:10.070 --> 11:10.830
Three seconds.

11:10.830 --> 11:11.430
Two minutes.

11:11.430 --> 11:12.480
Ninety seconds.

11:12.480 --> 11:13.550
Understood.

11:13.550 --> 11:14.780
Thank ya.

11:15.310 --> 11:16.280
Don't move!

11:17.240 --> 11:18.900
Don't try anything funny.

11:38.480 --> 11:39.250
Huh?

11:45.520 --> 11:47.180
You can drive?!

11:47.390 --> 11:49.840
I was a driver when I was younger!

11:49.840 --> 11:51.310
Ever heard of the Sonic Lady?

11:51.310 --> 11:53.060
Well, that's me!

11:59.730 --> 12:02.280
One hundred twenty seconds. 
You're over by thirty.

12:02.280 --> 12:03.090
Stickler.

12:03.090 --> 12:04.760
Try to be punctual, please.

12:04.760 --> 12:05.650
Hey!

12:06.290 --> 12:07.510
What the hell did you guys do?!

12:10.120 --> 12:11.690
It just grazed you.

12:11.690 --> 12:14.100
Be glad that was only a stray bullet.

12:14.100 --> 12:14.920
Are you all right?

12:14.920 --> 12:16.390
You useless trash!

12:16.390 --> 12:18.380
Can't you even protect your master?!

12:18.380 --> 12:19.760
You got shot too, didn't you?

12:22.280 --> 12:25.590
All the bullets passed through, 
and your intake unit is undamaged.

12:25.590 --> 12:26.390
You'll be fine.

12:27.420 --> 12:29.230
The correct answer was "a doctor"?

12:30.540 --> 12:31.730
There's a forest over there!

12:31.950 --> 12:32.900
Perfect!

12:38.710 --> 12:42.080
Better hold on tight, or you'll be thrown out!

12:51.780 --> 12:52.800
It's no use.

12:52.800 --> 12:54.760
The cable's completely shot.

12:54.760 --> 12:56.150
So what are you gonna do?!

12:56.150 --> 12:58.760
I need to get to Wellstown today!

12:59.160 --> 13:02.730
There should be a military facility 
left over from the war up ahead.

13:03.210 --> 13:05.040
We might find replacement parts there.

13:05.040 --> 13:06.670
I'll go look.

13:06.670 --> 13:08.290
You're quite knowledgeable.

13:08.290 --> 13:10.020
I'm a history-loving military nerd.

13:10.720 --> 13:12.690
It's an RG200 cable.

13:12.690 --> 13:14.070
One just like this.

13:14.070 --> 13:15.170
Roger.

13:15.170 --> 13:17.020
You're going with her!

13:17.210 --> 13:18.130
Huh?!

13:18.130 --> 13:19.070
Me, too.

13:20.430 --> 13:21.770
I'll go, too.

13:21.770 --> 13:23.460
You stay here.

13:23.460 --> 13:23.990
Huh?

13:24.730 --> 13:25.630
I'm going.

13:25.630 --> 13:27.810
And what if those guys come back?

13:28.150 --> 13:29.520
Rouge! House!

13:30.230 --> 13:31.810
Grr...

13:33.080 --> 13:33.950
Woof!

13:35.080 --> 13:37.420
Nice! When did you get this shot?

13:37.870 --> 13:39.760
I think these guys are SOA.

13:39.760 --> 13:41.320
SOA?

13:41.630 --> 13:44.430
Suns of Ares. SOA for short.

13:44.620 --> 13:47.460
A private security company—
or in other words, mercenaries.

13:47.460 --> 13:49.060
It means someone hired them.

13:49.660 --> 13:50.930
Yo. Hey.

13:51.410 --> 13:53.810
Still, this really is a great shot.

13:54.360 --> 13:56.300
You could win a Pulitzer Prize with this.

13:56.300 --> 13:58.580
I can take pictures like that, too!

13:58.580 --> 14:00.640
You're still too little for that.

14:01.870 --> 14:03.040
Wait!

14:04.560 --> 14:08.260
I guess what you said about going after 
bad guys wasn't just make-believe.

14:08.610 --> 14:09.570
It was.

14:10.020 --> 14:11.810
You saved my skin.

14:12.260 --> 14:12.990
Thanks.

14:15.130 --> 14:18.740
I just... follow orders. That's all.

14:19.370 --> 14:20.880
You're free.

14:22.400 --> 14:23.320
Free?

14:23.940 --> 14:24.830
Me?

14:25.220 --> 14:27.010
"Free" means you can make your own choices.

14:27.380 --> 14:28.340
Right?

14:40.830 --> 14:44.570
Let's take a great picture and prove to 
your brother that you're not too little.

14:46.200 --> 14:46.940
Yeah!

14:47.300 --> 14:48.060
Let's go!

14:55.950 --> 14:57.020
There's a person!

14:57.720 --> 14:58.500
A Nean.

14:59.270 --> 15:02.760
One who fought alongside humans, huh?

15:07.700 --> 15:09.130
Thank you.

15:18.400 --> 15:19.590
What is that?

15:20.680 --> 15:22.440
A Usurper war machine.

15:25.310 --> 15:27.000
Also known as a Cylinder Head.

15:31.110 --> 15:33.360
If it's not turned on...

15:34.810 --> 15:36.160
It's just scrap.

15:37.150 --> 15:38.420
What are you doing?

15:39.580 --> 15:41.380
Inspecting battlefield wreckage.

15:41.950 --> 15:45.240
This whole area was the 
site of a fierce battle.

15:46.340 --> 15:48.140
This one's dead, too.

15:48.140 --> 15:50.070
Won't get any money out of this.

15:50.640 --> 15:51.450
Who are you?

15:56.790 --> 15:57.940
Emily!

15:58.450 --> 15:59.960
Emily!

15:59.960 --> 16:00.970
What's wrong?

16:00.970 --> 16:02.940
I can't find Emily.

16:03.810 --> 16:05.980
Huh? Wait, is Rouge missing, too?

16:06.310 --> 16:07.680
She didn't run away, did she?!

16:20.830 --> 16:21.580
Emily?!

16:25.060 --> 16:26.290
Don't move!

16:26.820 --> 16:29.760
This type reacts to movement.

16:30.630 --> 16:32.300
Just hold still and keep quiet.

16:32.560 --> 16:35.060
It'll go back into sleep mode eventually.

16:37.000 --> 16:38.240
Uh...

16:41.870 --> 16:42.670
Run!

16:58.670 --> 16:59.580
Found her!

16:59.580 --> 17:02.040
That's... a Cylinder Head!

17:12.650 --> 17:13.390
What's that?

17:13.810 --> 17:15.070
Emily...

17:30.230 --> 17:32.330
Damn it! How is it so—

18:06.520 --> 18:07.400
It can't be...

18:11.120 --> 18:11.940
Emily!

18:12.990 --> 18:13.860
Rouge?!

18:15.910 --> 18:16.690
Huh?

18:18.130 --> 18:19.160
The repair's done!

18:21.710 --> 18:22.830
Move! Quick!

18:22.830 --> 18:24.300
There's a nasty one coming!

18:24.670 --> 18:25.490
Who are you?

18:29.240 --> 18:30.250
You're kidding me...

18:36.920 --> 18:38.000
Time to move!

18:51.690 --> 18:53.190
Rouge! Where were you?!

18:53.190 --> 18:54.610
It deflected it?!

18:59.580 --> 19:02.680
Stick closer! Get inside the barrier!

19:02.680 --> 19:04.830
You and your selfish demands!

19:08.230 --> 19:09.930
Hang on!

20:33.800 --> 20:35.860
Hey, where's Rouge?

20:36.290 --> 20:38.300
Maybe we should go back.

20:38.620 --> 20:40.340
Eh, I'm sure it'll be fine.

20:40.700 --> 20:43.220
Hey, I like that.

20:44.200 --> 20:45.280
Who <i>are</i> you?

20:55.770 --> 20:58.190
You took this? It's awesome!

21:01.260 --> 21:05.360
I have an older brother, too, 
so I know how you feel.

21:06.030 --> 21:06.920
Thank you!

21:10.830 --> 21:12.550
You're a real grown-up now.

21:13.140 --> 21:17.650
The precious little child went out into the 
world and climbed the stairs to adulthood.

21:17.650 --> 21:18.620
So it goes.
